>
  <h2>Selected Work</h2>
  <p class="lead-text">
    I'm a founding engineer at Thea, and the work I can show publicly is my own projects.
  </p>

  <div class="work-list">
    <article class="work-item">
      <h3><a href="/work/parkking/" class="text-link">ParkKing — Toronto Curb Parking Platform</a></h3>
      <p>
        An end-to-end system that turns Toronto's parking bylaws, written as legal prose, into curb-level rules and a free iPhone app that answers "can I park here?" for any time you choose, with no network needed:
      </p>
      <ul class="work-subcomponents">
        <li><strong>Data pipeline</strong>: Python, GeoPandas and Shapely. Parses bylaw text for schedules and street spans, resolves them against the City's street network, and projects them onto physical curbs. A release carries about 82,000 curb features, plus ticket-derived paid-curb labels and ticket-risk estimates.</li>
        <li><strong>iPhone app</strong>: Native SwiftUI and MapKit with no third-party dependencies. A bundled SQLite database with a spatial index and an on-device verdict engine. Live on the App Store.</li>
        <li><strong>Android app</strong>: A Kotlin and Jetpack Compose port of the same verdict engine, in development.</li>
      </ul>
      <ul class="work-tags" aria-label="Technologies used">
        <li>Python</li>
        <li>GeoPandas &amp; Shapely</li>
        <li>SwiftUI</li>
        <li>MapKit</li>
        <li>Kotlin</li>
        <li>SQLite</li>
        <li>Spatial ETL</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="work-links">
        <a href="/work/parkking/">Read Case Study &rarr;</a>
